                                "sense_id": "70392a56-58c0-3fd0-adcf-000969060791",
                                "text": "And when Phineas the sonne of Eleazer the sonne of Aaro the preast sawe it he rose vp out of the companye and toke a wepon in his hande"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c63ef602-0d00-49cf-97f2-e2e5f57b0b46",
                                "sense_id": "70392a56-58c0-3fd0-adcf-000969060791",
                                "text": "And we'll rub up our old Latin, and dip into modern poetry—great rubbish, I fear! Nobody like our old friend Will of Avon, or even your namesake, worthy Phineas Fletcher."
                            }
                        ]
